{# ===========================================================================
   Layout: base

   The shell every page in the main template family hangs off. Provides the
   document head, the theme attributes, the skip link, the site header, the
   <main> landmark, and the monolith footer.

   Front matter a page may set:
     title            required, the <title> tag (unique per page)
     description      required, meta description (unique per page)
     bodyClass        optional, page-level hook class on <body>
     schema           optional, a JSON-LD object rendered into the head
     noindex          optional, true to suppress indexing
     heroImage        optional, path to the LCP image, emits a preload
     mode             optional, pins this page's theme, overriding site.json

   v2: light and dark both ship, day is the default, and the toggle is manual
   (no clock, no prefers-color-scheme). site.theme.mode is the server-rendered
   default and the no-JS answer; components/theme-init.njk corrects it from
   localStorage before first paint. See DESIGN_SYSTEM.md.

   `mode` pins a page to one theme. Nothing uses it now that every page runs
   the v2 ramp; it stays because a page may legitimately need to pin one.
   =========================================================================== #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html
  lang="{{ site.locale }}"
  data-mode="{{ mode | default(site.theme.mode) }}"
  data-fonts="{{ site.theme.fonts }}"
  data-pattern="{{ site.theme.pattern }}">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

  {% include "components/theme-init.njk" %}

  <title>{{ title }}</title>
  <meta name="description" content="{{ description }}">

  {# Self-referencing canonical on every page. UTM params are stripped at the
     Cloudflare edge and 301'd to the clean URL. See SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md. #}
  <link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.url }}{{ page.url }}">
  {#- PREVIEW BRANCH: the whole build is noindex, unconditionally. The
      per-page `noindex` flag still applies on main; here it is irrelevant
      because nothing on this deploy may be indexed. Backed by an
      X-Robots-Tag on /* in public/_headers and a blanket robots.txt, so it
      survives a template refactor. -#}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">

  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.circulationstudio.com" crossorigin>
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bebas+Neue&family=Barlow+Condensed:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,600;0,700;1,600&family=Barlow:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet">

  <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">

  {#
    LCP preload. CLAUDE.md Performance Standards: a hero image gets
    loading="eager", fetchpriority="high" AND a preload. The first two live on
    the <img>; only this one needs the document head, which is why it is a
    front-matter field rather than something a page can do for itself.

    Set `heroImage` only on the one image that is actually the LCP element.
    Preloading anything below the fold competes with the real LCP for
    bandwidth and makes the metric worse, not better.
  #}
  {%- if heroImage %}
  <link rel="preload" as="image" href="{{ heroImage }}" fetchpriority="high">
  {%- endif %}

  {# Vite resolves this module entry and the stylesheet it imports, then
     rewrites both to hashed assets. See eleventy.config.js. #}
  <script type="module" src="/src/js/main.js"></script>

  {#
    One <script type="application/ld+json"> per page, holding a single @graph.
    Graphs are built in _data/schema.js from the same data the page renders,
    and selected by the page's `pageKey` front matter.
  #}
  {#- Paginated location stubs pick their graph by location id, since they all
      share one pageKey. Everything else selects by pageKey. -#}
  {%- if pageKey == "locationStub" %}
    {%- set pageSchema = schema.locationPages[loc.id] %}
  {%- elif pageKey %}
    {%- set pageSchema = schema[pageKey] %}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if pageSchema %}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ pageSchema | dump | safe }}</script>
  {%- endif %}
</head>

<body{% if bodyClass %} class="{{ bodyClass }}"{% endif %}>

  {% include "components/preview-banner.njk" %}

  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  {% include "components/site-header.njk" %}

  <main id="main">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </main>

  {% include "components/monolith.njk" %}

</body>
</html>
